    "In Class 13 we built a first passing network! Yay.\n",
    "\n",
    "Today we slow that object down and make it more rigorous. A passing network sits in a useful middle ground between a raw event log and a one-number team summary: it keeps relational structure visible while still giving us something we can inspect, visualize, and measure (Duch, Waitzman, and Amaral 2010; López Peña and Touchette 2012). At the same time, reviews of football network analysis stress that space, time, substitutions, and opponent interaction cannot be treated as afterthoughts (Ribeiro et al. 2017; Buldú et al. 2018; Caicedo-Parada, Lago-Peñas, and Ortega-Toro 2020)."
