    "The literature is very clear on this point: football passing networks are useful precisely because they summarize interaction structure, but they remain abstractions of a much richer game (Ribeiro et al. 2017; Buldú et al. 2018; Caicedo-Parada, Lago-Peñas, and Ortega-Toro 2020).\n",
    "\n",
    "Other legitimate network designs are possible. Nodes could be pitch zones rather than players, or role groups rather than named individuals, or player-time states in a dynamic network. Narizuka, Yamamoto, and Yamazaki (2014) show one influential spatial example. Today we keep the focus on *player passing networks*, and we keep most figures on the pitch because geography matters in soccer."
   ]
