    "## 3. Recap from last time: Event data\n",
    "\n",
    "StatsBomb event data is a **nested JSON event log**. Each row is one event in match order, but many fields are themselves dictionaries or lists. That nested structure is useful because a pass row needs to carry information about the passer, the intended recipient, the start and end locations, the pass type, the outcome, and more. Flattening too aggressively at the start can hide where these fields come from, so we will inspect the raw structure before we turn it into a DataFrame (StatsBomb 2019; StatsBomb 2026a).\n",
    "\n",
    "For passing networks, the most important fields are:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `type.name`\n",
    "- `team.name`\n",
    "- `player.name`\n",
    "- `pass.recipient.name`\n",
    "- `location`\n",
    "- `pass.end_location`\n",
    "- `pass.outcome.name`\n",
    "- `pass.type.name`\n",
    "- `period`\n",
    "- `minute`\n",
    "- `second`\n",
    "- `timestamp`\n"
   ]
