    "In this file, a completed pass is usually encoded by **missing** `pass.outcome.name`, while unsuccessful passes carry an explicit outcome value such as `Out`. That means `pass.outcome.name.isna()` is the right completion check **for this match file**.\n",
    "\n",
    "There is a second subtlety. Many ordinary passes have missing `pass.type.name`. Rather than silently dropping them, we relabel those missing values as `\"Regular\"` so that ordinary in-play passes remain visible. This is one of those small schema decisions that is easy to hide in code but worth stating explicitly.\n"
   ]
  },
