    "## 7. Node-level network analysis: several lenses on the same players\n",
    "\n",
    "A single pitch plot tells us something, but not everything. The same network can be read through several node-level properties. Here we will compute a compact set of measures directly in `networkx`, define each one, and then visualize the same passing network again and again with node sizes determined by different quantities.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a good place to slow down conceptually. A node measure is not a verdict about who was the “best player.” It is a statement about a player's **structural role in this particular graph**, under the modeling choices we already made (Ribeiro et al. 2017; Buldú et al. 2018; Caicedo-Parada, Lago-Peñas, and Ortega-Toro 2020).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
