    "So a player's score rises not only when they receive many passes, but when they receive them from teammates who themselves matter structurally. In code we use `nx.pagerank(G, weight=\"weight\")` (Page et al. 1999; NetworkX Developers 2025e).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Soccer intuition.** PageRank often highlights trusted circulation hubs or high-value receivers in the middle of the team's passing backbone.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Caveat.** Prestige in a passing network is not the same thing as attacking value.\n"
   ]
