    "### 7.6 HITS hub and authority scores: who acts more like a distributor, and who acts more like a sought-after target?\n",
    "\n",
    "The HITS algorithm assigns **two** scores to each node:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "h_i = \\sum_{i \\to j} a_j,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "a_i = \\sum_{j \\to i} h_j,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $h_i$ is node $i$'s **hub score** and $a_i$ is its **authority score** (Kleinberg 1999). In words:\n",
    "\n",
    "- a strong **hub** points to strong authorities,\n",
    "- a strong **authority** is pointed to by strong hubs.\n",
    "\n",
    "`networkx` implements this with `nx.hits(G)`. Because our graph already carries weighted edges, the weighted adjacency matrix is used by the algorithm.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Soccer intuition.** Hub score emphasizes a player's role as a distributor into important channels. Authority score emphasizes being a target found by structurally important distributors.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Caveat.** These labels come from web-link analysis, so we should read them as structural analogies rather than literal soccer roles.\n"
   ]
  },
