    "Several useful patterns appear immediately.\n",
    "\n",
    "Argentina's back line and deep midfield dominate many of the volume and brokerage measures, especially Nicolás Otamendi, Enzo Fernández, and Cristian Romero. That is not surprising when we remember that the baseline network is about **circulation structure**, not chance value. Lionel Messi matters in the match for reasons that a passing network only partly captures. Here he appears as an important receiver and connector, but not as the single maximal node on every measure. That is exactly the kind of grounded reading the reviews recommend: centrality is about role in the graph, not a shortcut for “best player” (Ribeiro et al. 2017; Buldú et al. 2018).\n",
    "\n",
    "The difference between neighboring measures also matters. Di María, for example, is more prominent on receiving-oriented measures than on pure outgoing volume, while Otamendi looks especially important on brokerage and outgoing distribution. The point is not to crown a winner among metrics. The point is to see that each metric asks a different structural question.\n"
   ]
  },
