    "## 10. Time and context matter\n",
    "\n",
    "One of the main lessons from the football network literature is that static full-match networks can hide large contextual changes (Buldú et al. 2018; Caicedo-Parada, Lago-Peñas, and Ortega-Toro 2020). This match is an ideal example.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will examine three kinds of variation:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. completed passes versus attempted passes with a known intended recipient,\n",
    "2. first half versus second half,\n",
    "3. and coarse time windows and score states across periods $1$ through $4$.\n",
    "\n",
    "For the first-half baseline comparison, we kept **starter-only** nodes for comparability. For later phase comparisons, we will usually allow **all players who actually appear in that phase**, because otherwise substitutes disappear from the network entirely.\n"
   ]
  },
