    "### 10.1 Completed passes versus attempted passes with a known recipient\n",
    "\n",
    "A completed-pass network describes **realized circulation**. An attempted-pass network with a known intended recipient answers a different question: who tried to connect with whom, even if the attempt failed.\n",
    "\n",
    "One plotting detail matters here. Failed passes do not create a true reception location, so for attempted-pass networks we keep the same location logic that uses pass origins plus successful receptions only. That avoids pretending that every attempted end location is a genuine on-ball receiving point.\n"
   ]
  },
